Minato (M6 a step 3, ADR-0053): nterp decodes references. A reference is the low 32 bits of the object's address
in the heap window (heap_window.h), so a reference that was only loaded must become an address before it is used as
one: DECODE_REF (orr xN, x20, xN, with the window's base in x20, in place and harmless on an address) after the
explicit null test; DECODE_REF_OR_NULL where C++ takes the pointer and null must stay null. Encoding costs nothing.
